{title: The Last Will Be First}
{subtitle: Matthew 20:1–16}
{key: C}
{tempo: 103}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [C] | [C] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Early in the morning, the landowner went
To hire some workers, a denarius was meant
At the third hour, at the sixth and the ninth
He went to the marketplace, he called them in line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
At the eleventh hour some were standing around
Why have you been standing here idle all day
Because no one has hired us, the men all replied
You also go into the vineyard, he said with a smile
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So the last will be [F]first
And the [C]first last [G]
Grace [Am]is not wages
Grace [F]is a gift that [C]holds [G][C]fast
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When evening came, they lined up for pay
The last ones got a denarius for one hour of the day
The first ones grumbled, we bore the scorching heat
Friend, I am doing you no wrong, take what is yours and eat
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So the last will be [F]first
And the [C]first [G]last
Grace [Am]is not wages
Grace [F]is a gift that [C]holds [G]fast
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [C] | [F] | [C] | [G] |
| [Am] | [F] | [C] | [G] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Am]Am I not allowed to do [F]what I want with what is [C]mine
Or are you envious be[G]cause I am generous
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So [C]the last will be first
And the first last
{end_of_verse}

